# Environment Variables Example
# Copy this file to .env for local development.

# Vite Configuration
VITE_APP_NAME=CrushLearn AI
VITE_APP_VERSION=1.0.0

# The AI gateway (see gateway/README.md) is a separate server-side process
# that holds the provider key. Its settings are read from the environment of
# THAT process, not from this file.
#
# Never put an AI provider key in a VITE_ variable: Vite embeds every
# VITE_* value into the browser bundle, which would ship the key to every
# browser that loads the page.
#
# Set the key in the gateway process's environment instead:
#
#   export ANTHROPIC_API_KEY="sk-ant-..."   # macOS / Linux
#   $env:ANTHROPIC_API_KEY = "sk-ant-..."   # Windows PowerShell
#   npm run dev:gateway
#
# The app runs without the gateway. It then answers from its local extractive
# path and says so in the chat panel.

# Where the browser finds the gateway. The dev server proxies /api to
# http://127.0.0.1:8787 by default, so this is usually unnecessary. It names a
# location, not a secret, so it is safe in the client bundle.
# VITE_GATEWAY_URL=
